  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsible Business Conduct and Horticulture Expertise</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the first quarter of 2021, The Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in Colombo, together with RVO, organised a series of webinars on Responsible Business Conduct (RBC) to raise awareness of the importance of RBC and adhering to the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises, promoting dialogue, building networks and engaging with stakeholders (active) in Sri Lanka (PSS20LK01). Indirectly, these webinars aimed to contribute to in-country policy developments and action to create an enabling environment for RBC. The Webinars contributed to an open dialogue among all relevant stakeholders. From the RBC webinar series and follow-up discussions, it became clear that awareness about RBC and its practical implications in different sectors is low for many Sri Lankan stakeholders. That is why the Embassy published an RBC handout to complement the Doing Business in Sri Lanka handbook (PSS21LK01a). There is an opportunity for EKN to become a frontrunner in integrating RBC into its business support in Sri Lanka. Within the scope of his project, capable experts, partners, possible activities and ways to ensure the continuation of what already started are identified.</narrative>
  </description>
